# Module development constraints

**Procedure and templates:** `docs/guides/MODULE_DEVELOPMENT_GUIDE.md`
**Contract authority:** `memory-bank/moduleSpecs.md` + `module-interoperability.mdc`

## Interoperability (non-negotiable)

- Same contract for built-in and marketplace modules: **`authorize → execute → emit normalized activity → notify/realtime`**; never emit on failed/unauthorized actions.
- Tenant scope on every persisted path; activity vs analytics separated; realtime membership proven before join/emit.

## Product integration

- Every business module must provide a workspace landing and register its canonical workspace rendering, icon, and display name before adding deep pages. Follow the guide’s current paths.
- User-facing deletes use **`trashedAt` soft delete**, exclude trashed records from lists, and integrate Global Trash; no hard delete except a documented exception.
- Ship an accurate, complete manifest with permissions and dependencies plus AI/notification metadata when applicable.

## AI context

- **If AI-exposed**, the module **must** ship a real **`ModuleAIContext`** (purpose, category, keywords, patterns, concepts, entities, actions, **`contextProviders`**) and at least one authenticated, fast, bounded `/api/.../ai/context/...` context provider — see `moduleSpecs.md` and `docs/guides/AI_CONTEXT_PROVIDER_API.md`.
- Modules that are **not** AI-exposed do **not** require AI context.
- If the module supports AI-driven writes, register an executor / supported operations per platform patterns. Read-only AI-exposed modules may omit executors.

## Notifications

- Types: **`[module]_[event]`**; use **`NotificationService.createNotification`**; manifest **`notifications`** metadata required for discovery.
- Update **`web/src/app/notifications/page.tsx`** and **`web/src/api/notifications.ts`** when adding types (see `docs/guides/NOTIFICATION_METADATA_GUIDE.md`).

## Certification

- First-party and marketplace review must apply the `moduleSpecs.md` certification checklist.
- Partner work must also follow `docs/guides/THIRD_PARTY_MODULE_PIPELINE_SOURCE_OF_TRUTH.md`.

